<title>USA: FGIC qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance Co. said on Wednesday that it qualified for bond insurance the following five issues scheduled for competitive sale:</p>
<p>--Folsom, Calif., $11.415 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Oakland, Calif., $22.25 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Santa Rosa High School District, Calif., $18.2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Reading Twp, N.J., $4.406 million general improvement.</p>
<p>--Albany City School District, N.Y., $13.975 million GOs.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
</text>
